00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.601
I'm happy that you're in New York City.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.767
We love you here. -Thank you.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.234
I love -- love being home.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:00.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.300
-If -- You know, today --

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.767
I was gonna ask you -- -Although it's changed a lot.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:06.601
Like, I'll go to my old neighborhood.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:08.400
I was in the -- I grew up in the hood,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.667
you know, on 16th Street and 9th Avenue.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:12.767
-Yeah.

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.200
-And back in the day it was the ghetto.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.133
But now everything is all gentrified.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.434
All my street cred is gone. I'll be like, "Yo, you know

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.968
where I'm from? I'm from Chelsea!"

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.934
They're like, "You talking about the meatpacking district?

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.167
Get yo' ass outta here."

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.234
-It's changed now. It's different now, yeah.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:29.901
-So different. -I was -- Today's 4/20.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.400
And I was going to ask you,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.334
because you've played stoners in a few of your films.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:35.400
